      "id": "concept_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Some objective questions ask for the number of prime factors after powers are expanded. Count repeated prime factors with multiplicity.\n\n12^3=(2^2×3)^3=2^6×3^3.\n\nThat contains 6+3=9 prime factors when repetitions are counted.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
