        "text": "In harder Surds and Indices questions, inspect before calculating.\n\nLook for a factor identity.\nLook for paired cube roots.\nCollect exponents before touching the base.\nRewrite powered integers into prime powers when counting factors.\nUse repeated difference of squares when factors double their exponents.\n\nName one long-looking expression from this lesson that became short after recognising its structure.",
